<!-- Listen-friendly content -->
<div class="listen-friendly-content" style="display: none;" aria-hidden="true">
  <div lang="en">
    <h2>Audio Summary: Dynamic-dLLM</h2>
    <p>Diffusion LLMs like LLaDA and Dream are powerful but slow — their computational cost scales as O(L cubed) because they cannot use KV-cache and must re-evaluate all tokens at every denoising step. Dynamic-dLLM is a training-free framework that addresses this with two adaptive components: Dynamic Cache Updating, which measures how much each layer's token representations change between steps and allocates cache-refresh budgets proportionally, and Adaptive Parallel Decoding, which tracks each token's confidence concentration and temporal stability to set a per-token commitment threshold that drops when predictions stabilize.</p>
    <p>On LLaDA-8B-Instruct, Dynamic-dLLM achieves 3.21 times average throughput improvement across five benchmarks, peaking at 4.48 times speedup on GSM8K math, all while maintaining near-baseline accuracy. The method generalizes to LLaDA-1.5 and Dream-v0-7B-Instruct with similar gains, and requires no fine-tuning — it is a fully plug-and-play solution.</p>
  </div>
  <div lang="zh">
    <h2>语音摘要：Dynamic-dLLM</h2>
    <p>LLaDA和Dream等扩散大语言模型功能强大，但速度较慢——其计算复杂度为O(L的三次方)，因为它们无法使用KV缓存，且必须在每个去噪步骤中重新计算所有标记。Dynamic-dLLM是一个无需训练的框架，通过两个自适应组件来解决这一问题：动态缓存更新（DCU），它测量每层标记表示在相邻步骤间的变化程度，并按比例分配缓存刷新预算；以及自适应并行解码（APD），它追踪每个标记的置信度集中度和时间稳定性，为每个标记设置动态承诺阈值，当预测趋于稳定时阈值降低。</p>
    <p>在LLaDA-8B-Instruct上，Dynamic-dLLM在五个基准测试上实现了平均3.21倍的吞吐量提升，在GSM8K数学推理任务上峰值达到4.48倍加速，同时保持接近基线的准确率。该方法无需任何微调，可直接应用于LLaDA-1.5和Dream-v0-7B-Instruct并取得相似的加速效果。</p>
  </div>
</div>
